admin-telemetry-title = Operational telemetry
admin-telemetry-help = Export operational traces and metrics to a collector compatible with OpenTelemetry, such as a self-hosted OpenTelemetry Collector. Export is off by default. Saved changes apply after restarting the server.
admin-telemetry-back = Back to observability
admin-telemetry-saved = Telemetry configuration saved. Restart the server to apply changes.
admin-telemetry-restart = The saved configuration differs from the running server. A restart is required.
admin-telemetry-reload = Reload configuration
admin-telemetry-save = Save telemetry configuration
admin-telemetry-collector = Collector and signals
admin-telemetry-collector-help = Only an administrator can choose this server-wide destination. Use a private collector or HTTPS; HTTP transmits telemetry without encryption.
admin-telemetry-enabled = Enable OTLP export
admin-telemetry-traces = Export traces
admin-telemetry-metrics = Export metrics
admin-telemetry-endpoint = OTLP gRPC endpoint
admin-telemetry-endpoint-help = Absolute HTTP or HTTPS collector address, usually port 4317. Do not include credentials, a query, or a fragment. This is a gRPC endpoint, not OTLP HTTP port 4318.
admin-telemetry-serviceName = Service name
admin-telemetry-serviceName-help = Stable service label used to identify this Mailwoman deployment in your collector. Do not use an email address or other personal information.
admin-telemetry-environment = Environment
admin-telemetry-environment-help = Optional deployment label such as production or staging. This is sent with exported telemetry.
admin-telemetry-pinned = Disabled fields are controlled by deployment environment variables. Change those variables to override their values.
admin-telemetry-limits = Sampling and export limits
admin-telemetry-limits-help = Bound memory and collector traffic. The batch size cannot exceed the queue size. Full queues can drop spans rather than block mail requests.
admin-telemetry-sampleRatio = Trace sampling ratio
admin-telemetry-sampleRatio-help = Fraction of new root traces to retain, from 0 to 1. Child spans follow the parent's sampling decision.
admin-telemetry-exportTimeoutMs = Export timeout (milliseconds)
admin-telemetry-exportTimeoutMs-help = Maximum duration of a collector export request, from 100 to 30000 milliseconds.
admin-telemetry-metricsIntervalSecs = Metrics interval (seconds)
admin-telemetry-metricsIntervalSecs-help = Time between metric exports, from 10 to 3600 seconds.
admin-telemetry-spanQueueSize = Span queue size
admin-telemetry-spanQueueSize-help = Maximum number of spans waiting for export, from 128 to 32768.
admin-telemetry-spanBatchSize = Span batch size
admin-telemetry-spanBatchSize-help = Maximum spans in one export, from 1 to 4096 and no greater than the queue size.
admin-telemetry-spanExportDelayMs = Span batch delay (milliseconds)
admin-telemetry-spanExportDelayMs-help = Normal wait between span batches, from 100 to 60000 milliseconds.
admin-telemetry-prometheus-help = A separate authenticated endpoint for a Prometheus-compatible scraper. Access always requires the deployment's MW_METRICS_TOKEN bearer token; its value is never returned to this page.
admin-telemetry-prometheusEnabled = Enable Prometheus scraping
admin-telemetry-token-missing = No scrape token is configured. The metrics endpoint remains inaccessible until the operator sets MW_METRICS_TOKEN.
